/// A package whose C defines the same names as the root's, the function
/// `helper`, the variable `total` and the alias `named`: each package's C
/// keeps its own, `defined_here`, which each package's interface header
/// defines itself, among them. `plain.h` includes nothing, not even
/// `<stdint.h>`. `once.h` defines functions, a variable, an alias and,
/// where the C library resolves one, an indirect function with external
/// linkage that `once.c`, which includes it, also defines, and a
/// constructor of the header's own: each is defined, and the constructor
/// run, once in the package's C, though the glue includes the header too.
/// A constructor of the header that sets up the header's private state,
/// which a `static inline` function the glue calls reads, runs for the
/// glue's copy of that state too, and so do one that sets it up through
/// a function of the header's it calls and one that sets it through a
/// pointer a variable of the header's holds.
/// `primed.h`, which no source includes, has constructors of its own, run
/// beside the one `lib.c` has, and beside the one `plain.c` has under the
/// same name and doing the same, which is not the header's.
/// `gnu.h` selects glibc's GNU features before it includes a system
/// header, which the glue keeps by including it before any of its own.
package lib;

alias I32 = @primitives$I32;
alias I64 = @primitives$I64;

I64 helper() foreign "helper";
I64 named() foreign "named";
I32 plus(a I32, b I32) foreign "plus";
I64 widen(x I64) foreign "widen";
I64 definedHere(x I64) foreign "defined_here";
I64 once(x I64) foreign "once";
I64 useOnce() foreign "use_once";
I64 onceAlias(x I64) foreign "once_alias";
I64 onceIndirect(x I64) foreign "once_indirect";
I64 onceStarted() foreign "once_started";
I64 onceValue() foreign "once_value";
I64 onceHelped() foreign "once_helped_value";
I64 oncePointed() foreign "once_pointed_value";
I64 primed() foreign "primed";
I64 primedRuns() foreign "primed_runs_seen";
I64 wasWarmed() foreign "was_warmed";
I64 parsed() foreign "parsed";
I64 gnuFound() foreign "gnu_found";
